data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"A persistent AVL tree appears suitable, allowing constant-time `BEGIN` operations via root node snapshotting. Exploring optimizations: In scenarios where a transaction commits with no other open transactions, in-place node mutation is possible. Version IDs on nodes, which determine their age relative to active snapshots, allows a hybrid approach combining in-place mutation and path-copying.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Initial calculations suggest memory usage scales linearly with the number of writes, with a focus on node allocation size. A mix of in-place mutation and path-copying seems reasonable for further optimization, as transient object allocation is expected during the write process. Checking read and range queries on snapshots, combined with a write list, is the next step.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The persistent BST (`snapshot`) provides logarithmic time complexity for reads: O(log S). Range queries require efficient computation of the count of keys within a range. Specifically, determine the count 'n' of keys in the range \\[lo, hi] within a transaction's view in O(log S + W) time, where W represents the number of writes in the transaction's write list.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The range query analysis concludes the complexity as O(log S + W), implying efficient retrieval times even for large datasets. Addressing conflict detection, revisiting the transaction constraints reveals the importance of precise conflict determination. The logic must ensure proper concurrency and data integrity, given the large-scale transaction requirements.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

