data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Rereading the requirements, I verified the condition `lo.compareTo(hi) <= 0` is required for valid range queries, and, if violated, is correctly handled. The read set and read ranges are append-only. No operations remove entries, and a `ROLLBACK` does not affect them, adhering to the requirements. Also, a transaction's own writes are not considered in the conflict detection.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The logic confirms that aborted transactions do not impact conflict detection, as they are excluded from `lastCommitMap` and `writtenKeysTree`. The `commitSeq` increments and these data structures update only upon successful transaction commit. This simplifies conflict resolution and maintains data integrity.\n\nThe maximum number of intact records in the 16 MiB input size calculates to approximately 2.8 million records, considering the smallest record size. This estimation accounts for the memory impact of the Java `Record`.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Initial calculations for record processing during Phase 1 were incorrect, resulting in overestimated memory usage. The structure of the `log` allows for direct processing of intact records without constructing intermediate Java objects. Phase 1 can directly determine record type and length from their offset.\n\nPhase 1 operates by iterating the log, skipping over bytes. The loop advances through valid records until an error is encountered. The record structure is read directly from the `log`, avoiding object instantiation to improve memory efficiency.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Phase 1 correctly identifies valid records by iterating the log and advancing the pointer based on record lengths, avoiding object instantiation and memory allocation. The logic confirms that the loop terminates precisely at the end of the intact records, verifying zero memory overhead.\n\nChecking `DUPLICATE_TXN`:\n - The `txn` value (u32) ranges from 1 to 4294967295, consistent with Java's integer representation.\n - The analysis considers the number of `BEGIN` records that can exist within the 16 MiB limit to address memory and speed concerns.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

