data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"A simple, open-addressing hash set (`int[]`) using Fibonacci hashing with a sentinel value of 0 appears sufficient for tracking transaction IDs, preventing adversarial collisions.  The sentinel value 0 is never assigned as a transaction ID due to the constraint R14. This reduces memory overhead compared to `HashSet`. The structure is re-sized as needed.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"`R17` (applied after `R14`) requires checking for duplicate transaction IDs, which necessitates a fast lookup structure. An integer hash set, initialized as `int[]` with `0` as the sentinel value, using Fibonacci hashing guarantees O(1) lookups and significantly reduces memory overhead with no object allocations.\n\nNext, I need to collect committed and aborted transaction IDs for the result. Since a maximum of approximately 930,000 transaction pairs (BEGIN/COMMIT) can fit within the 16 MiB limit (each entry: 9 bytes), I will collect these IDs in a `long[]` array. Returning a `List<Long>` can be done efficiently with `AbstractList<Long>` (implementing `RandomAccess`) backed by this `long[]`.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"A `long[]` array is used to collect committed and aborted transaction IDs during replay, as standard `ArrayList<Long>` would exceed the memory limit. Dynamically collect transaction IDs into a primitive `int[]` array. After replay (if no exceptions), build an `ArrayList<Long>` using the primitive array to construct the `Result` list of `Long` transaction IDs, ensuring standard Java collection behavior.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"A careful review of string encoding requirements (Section 5.3) and valid byte ranges for keys and values confirms that all characters are within the Latin-1 range.  This enables the direct use of the `ISO_8859_1` encoding. Compact Strings are suitable for efficiency. `String` creation involves `new String(log, keyOffset, k, StandardCharsets.ISO_8859_1)`.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

