data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Initial skepticism regarding immutable result requirements. Verification revealed that standard `HashMap` and `ArrayList` returns are acceptable, no unmodifiable structures are enforced. Focusing on handling edge cases for truncated logs, re-examining the constraints R3 and R4.\n\nR3 and R4 are confirmed for empty, truncated logs. Valid magic values ('WAL1') were verified. An empty log results in `validLength=0` with `tornTail = false`.\nLogs shorter than 4 bytes, matching the initial bytes of \"WAL1,\" are now handled. Invalid magic byte sequences now trigger appropriate `WalException` errors. Phase 1 processing starts correctly when the magic bytes are valid.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Iterating through the log, the analysis correctly addresses truncated records and implements checks for type and length validation (R5-R9), with careful consideration of potential integer overflows during length calculations. Specifically, the length check handles all `L` values up to `Integer.MAX_VALUE` using an explicit length comparison to avoid potential integer overflow. The updated record processing logic now thoroughly validates frame types and lengths.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The checksum calculation's modulo operation requires careful verification. Initial skepticism regarding potential overflow was correct. Detailed analysis confirmed the range of `s1` and `b`, ensuring `s1 + b` never exceeds `509`, validating the modulo operation and avoiding subtle errors. Further optimization is not needed, as `3 + n <= 1027`, further guaranteeing correctness.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

