data: {"id":"chatcmpl-689b7469-a194-4d8e-ab6b-cfd8bb69e42a","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795554462,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Initial suspicion was a memory leak in the AVL tree due to incorrect height updates during rotations, which led to incorrect size fields. Thoroughly reviewed each of the four AVL rotation cases to confirm that the `height` and `size` fields are updated correctly. The AVL tree is correctly handling all of its data.\n\nThe `StringIntMap` is crucial for conflict detection. The implementation uses a high-performance open-addressing hash table with primitive arrays, avoiding object creation and ensuring O(1) average lookup. Collision risks are mitigated by dynamically resizing the table.\n\nFocusing now on the test logic of the data structures. The current code is now correct.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

